WEBVTT

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:34.510
Midday Moon

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:39.140
What the hell is that?!

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:39.890
GRRR

00:01:39.890 --> 00:01:41.850
Enough! I'm going!

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:46.060
So where is that middle school?
What's the name of that homeroom teacher?!

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:51.190
I can understand why that big sister is worried!

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.570
From what I've heard,
that homeroom teacher is rotten to the core!

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:55.950
FACULTY ROOM

00:01:55.570 --> 00:01:57.700
Mr. Hayashida! Calm down!

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.490
<i>Don't raise your voice to me.</i>

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:03.750
I should really go!

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:05.580
Just let me go, Kiriyama!

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:07.330
Mr. Hayashida, relax!

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:12.800
As a fellow teacher, there's something
I want to say to that homeroom teacher!

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.590
I know what you mean because I...

00:02:17.180 --> 00:02:18.930
I want to go too!

00:02:19.340 --> 00:02:20.430
But...

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:23.430
...I don't have the knowledge.

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:25.310
I can't be of any help.

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:35.820
In my own case, I would pretend to be fine

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:37.450
and just isolate myself.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:42.780
I didn't bother to struggle,
but just endure it and go with the flow,

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.490
escaping into shogi...

00:02:47.830 --> 00:02:52.000
So I don't have any useful wisdom
for a time like this!

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:54.090
I thought if I could...

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.970
...at least make money by winning matches,

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:04.010
they could put it to good use for something,
so I tried my best.

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:13.980
But they aren't the kind of people who would
accept money from a total stranger like me.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:17.990
So please tell me, Mr. Hayashida!

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:20.490
I'll treat you to oden or yakiniku or anything!

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:21.870
Please lend me your wisdom!

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:27.040
You moron!

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.330
Kiriyama!

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.120
HEEHEE

00:03:28.330 --> 00:03:29.660
"Please do me a favor."

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:31.330
"I'll buy you a drink later."

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.790
Quit talking like a damn salaryman!

00:03:31.540 --> 00:03:33.790
SLAP

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:36.800
*Looks like he can't speak

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:40.760
Certainly you've been working hard

00:03:40.760 --> 00:03:45.310
and maybe make more money than me,
which sometimes pisses me off,

00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:47.970
but this is a school,

00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:50.190
and you're just
a second-year high school student.

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:51.940
I'm a teacher!

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:54.940
Don't underestimate a teacher!

00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:05.490
First, I think Hina should change
the person she's talking to.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:10.210
Like the head teacher
or the teacher of another subject...

00:04:11.410 --> 00:04:13.580
Her homeroom teacher
isn't the only option at school.

00:04:13.830 --> 00:04:17.460
If that doesn't work,
it's okay for her to talk to another teacher.

00:04:18.170 --> 00:04:22.630
And about speaking to the bully's parents...

00:04:24.140 --> 00:04:27.470
Yeah, I don't think it would go that far.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:28.970
Not in this situation.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:32.560
But if it does come to that,

00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:35.770
it's true that the big sister alone
would feel helpless.

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.480
Their mother passed away, right?

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.490
What about the father? What's he doing?

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.740
Well...

00:04:50.410 --> 00:04:54.250
It's not a very pleasant story,
so I'll just give you the basics.

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:58.170
He told us he got a new girlfriend...

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:00.420
...and then just left us.

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:04.300
Now he's living in a new home
and has another child.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:09.600
Oh, that's right.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:12.060
We have bean jam pancakes. Want some?

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:14.690
Sure.

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:17.520
Thank you.

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:21.400
<i>It's as if...</i>

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:25.950
<i>she laid it out so it can mean nothing to her.</i>

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:30.410
<i>But I realized Akari's heart
was floating around,</i>

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:33.080
<i>unable to find a place to rest.</i>

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:37.080
<i>It wasn't that it was nothing to her.</i>

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.960
<i>She still only talks about it
as if it meant nothing to her.</i>

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:42.840
<i>Still.</i>

00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.590
I see.

00:05:50.720 --> 00:05:52.850
All the more reason that I have to go!

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.940
How do you get that from this?

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:58.440
In fact, how would you even
announce yourself when you arrive?

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:02.530
RUMBLE
RUMBLE

00:05:58.770 --> 00:06:02.530
As "Hina's friend's former homeroom teacher,"
of course!

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:04.990
That equals "perfect stranger!"

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:08.450
Mr. Hayashida, you've already become
a "monster teacher!"

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:09.320
GRRRRR

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:11.330
If the bully will bring out her MPs...

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.330
*MP = Short for "Monster Parents"

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:12.080
SPURT

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.330
...then we'll release the MT!

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:14.330
*MT = Short for "Monster Teacher"

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.580
Am I wrong? I'm not wrong, damn it!

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:21.460
One would be as bad as the other...
Or are you even worse?

00:06:18.380 --> 00:06:21.460
*In terms of being a total stranger!!

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:23.710
Help!

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:25.470
Oh yeah, also...

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:30.100
About the money issue,
I'm glad you realized the futility yourself.

00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:32.350
I'm relieved by that, sheesh.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.770
When I thought about you going there

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:37.600
with your bank book and having
a budget committee for another family...

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:39.230
...I was nervous.

00:06:39.520 --> 00:06:41.610
I thought they might slam the door
in your face, Kiriyama.

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:44.980
SHAKE
SHAKE

00:06:42.610 --> 00:06:44.980
Was planning to do
just that

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:56.000
<i>On the way home, Mr. Hayashida
bought me a steamed meat bun,</i>

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:57.830
<i>explaining it as his "pride as a teacher."</i>

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:05.170
<i>And then he accused me
of being "out of step" and stubborn.</i>

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:12.180
<i>And then he patted me on the back.</i>

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.520
<i>"Wanting to be needed."
"Therefore, wanting to be strong."</i>

00:07:24.270 --> 00:07:26.940
<i>He said, "What's so wrong with that?"</i>

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:33.370
The calm mind is the way

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:36.240
<i>He said, "First, all you can do...</i>

00:07:36.410 --> 00:07:37.370
Let's have a good game.

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:43.670
<i>...is what you can do, one thing at a time."</i>

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:51.260
<i>He told me to take a deep breath,</i>

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:56.640
<i>then start walking, a step at a time.</i>

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:10.150
I lost.

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:13.990
Thank you.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:22.460
Hey, Kiriyama.

00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:24.040
Oh, Mr. Yokomizo.

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:29.050
Kishou Battle
Rei Kiriyama
Ichirou Morita

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:29.050
Kiryu Battle
Keita Kurasawa
Santa Mine

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:27.550
Three white stars. You're in fine form.

00:08:27.880 --> 00:08:29.050
Thank you.

00:08:29.420 --> 00:08:33.050
So your opponent in the Newcomer
Tournament finals is Junkei Yamazaki, huh?

00:08:33.550 --> 00:08:36.550
Good luck. Do it for Nikaidou too.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:41.810
I will.

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:44.440
Hachiya / Kiriyama

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:44.440
Yamazaki / Nikaidou

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:44.440
Newcomer Tournament

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.560
Kiriyama

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.560
Yamazaki

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.560
Newcomer Tournament

00:08:46.900 --> 00:08:48.570
<i>Don't lose along the way!</i>

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:52.700
<i>Because you and I are going to create a legend!</i>

00:08:58.950 --> 00:09:00.120
Idiot...

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.620
After drilling that into my head,
again and again...

00:09:05.500 --> 00:09:06.630
Nikaidou...

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:12.470
So what's going on with Nikaidou?

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:16.470
He can't return from Osaka for a while?

00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:21.180
Yes. He's been admitted
to the Osaka First Central Hospital.

00:09:21.470 --> 00:09:23.980
He'll be there a while for observation.

00:09:24.980 --> 00:09:26.730
Apparently it's difficult to move him closer.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:29.520
Mr. Shimada.

00:09:29.940 --> 00:09:30.980
What...

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:33.700
Kiriyama.

00:09:38.780 --> 00:09:40.330
...are you talking about?

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:44.000
Midday Moon

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:48.000
Adventurers

00:09:51.050 --> 00:09:54.010
What are you talking about?

00:09:54.970 --> 00:09:57.510
Nikaidou... is in the hospital?

00:09:58.090 --> 00:09:59.180
Did something happen?

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:05.440
<i>The expression
on the adults' faces read "Oh, shoot"</i>

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:07.480
<i>and I figured it out right away.</i>

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.440
<i>That I was the only one who didn't know.</i>

00:10:13.030 --> 00:10:14.440
It's nothing major.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.820
He wasn't well to begin with,

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:22.080
so the strain of the Newcomer Tournament
semi-finals made his condition worse.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:25.910
That's right.
Come on, Shimada, let's get that drink.

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.300
Please, wait!

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:44.810
If this was his usual health downswing,

00:10:44.810 --> 00:10:49.150
that limousine with a bed
or whatever could take him back here, right?

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:51.190
He still has rank-deciding matches!

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.780
But if he's in the hospital for a while...

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:57.200
Is it that bad?

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:00.490
Kiriyama...

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:11.460
If you ask me and I can't answer,
there must be a reason, right?

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:16.090
You should understand that much.

00:11:22.470 --> 00:11:24.600
<i>The truth is I'd been faintly aware of it.</i>

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:29.730
<i>Mr. Hanaoka, who was always at his side,</i>

00:11:30.690 --> 00:11:33.730
<i>the beautifully decorated,
faintly colored lunches,</i>

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:37.740
<i>all of the medications
he always had in his bag...</i>

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:42.490
<i>The truth is I could never bring myself
to ask about it.</i>

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:49.960
<i>Ever since we were kids,
I knew Nikaidou didn't like to be asked about it.</i>

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.340
Is that so?

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:55.630
In that case...

00:11:57.210 --> 00:12:01.130
...could I ask you what the reason itself is,
along with everything else?

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:12.650
Shimada, I'm going home.

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.480
Take care of things.

00:12:18.690 --> 00:12:19.940
Kiriyama.

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:24.370
SHOGI HALL

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:22.910
Why don't we grab dinner?

00:12:29.450 --> 00:12:33.710
<i>After that, Mr. Shimada
talked to me about Nikaidou.</i>

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:38.130
<i>He talked about his disciple
and his "little brother."</i>

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:43.340
You're taking on another disciple?

00:12:45.100 --> 00:12:46.010
Yeah.

00:12:46.680 --> 00:12:51.140
Sensei, you've always said that
I would be your last disciple.

00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:55.150
And you got sick last year, so why now?

00:12:57.110 --> 00:13:01.650
Well, the thing is, I found an interesting child.

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:10.080
<i>To become a shogi professional,
you have to first join the association.</i>

00:13:10.500 --> 00:13:14.920
<i>And to do that,
you have to be under someone's wing.</i>

00:13:15.040 --> 00:13:16.540
TINY

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:21.050
<i>And so, a fourth-grader came over.</i>

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:22.550
SHINE

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:23.300
Nice to meet you!

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:25.550
I'm Harunobu Nikaidou!

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:32.180
This is Shimada 6th-Dan.
He's your big brother.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:35.480
You two get along now.

00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:37.440
He's so round.

00:13:38.150 --> 00:13:40.440
<i>Huh? Where have I...</i>

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:44.450
<i>I remembered him from somewhere.</i>

00:13:44.450 --> 00:13:47.450
CHILDREN'S SHOGI TOURNAMENT

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:56.960
<i>I'd seen him when I was a guest lecturer
at a children's tournament.</i>

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:03.380
What's with the round kid?

00:14:03.380 --> 00:14:05.220
Making an old man carry his lunch...

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:08.350
I heard he pulled up in a fancy car.

00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:09.850
What a stuck-up.

00:14:10.470 --> 00:14:14.060
This is probably a rich kid's pastime.
He won't be around for long.

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:31.910
- Now chew well. Thirty times each bite.
- Okay.

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:37.250
<i>A special lunch, huh?</i>

00:14:38.630 --> 00:14:40.250
<i>Spoiled rich kid.</i>

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:46.380
<i>Why go to all the trouble of entering this world?</i>

00:14:46.720 --> 00:14:50.180
<i>I'm sure his parents would buy him
whatever manga or video games he wanted.</i>

00:14:51.930 --> 00:14:56.890
<i>I was envious of him,
since I lived in poverty when I was a kid.</i>

00:14:57.810 --> 00:15:00.480
<i>Well, I'm sure he won't stick with it.</i>

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:03.360
<i>Video games and computers are more fun.</i>

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:08.150
CHILDREN'S SHOGI TOURNAMENT

00:15:04.110 --> 00:15:08.150
Thank you for your patience.
It's now time for the final match.

00:15:08.530 --> 00:15:11.830
From Suginami Ward, Tokyo, Rei Kiriyama!

00:15:15.080 --> 00:15:18.160
So the spoiled rich kid lost in the semi-finals.

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:22.670
He did better than I expected.

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:27.670
<i>I was shocked when I saw the game records.</i>

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:32.430
Wh-What is this? All-out war,
with both of them having sitting kings?

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:34.810
And 185 moves...

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:37.680
Is this really elementary school shogi?

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:42.810
Is he okay? I'll call an ambulance.

00:15:44.860 --> 00:15:48.530
He'll be fine.
There's no need for an ambulance.

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:51.200
The car is waiting downstairs.

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:55.120
<i>From the old man's calm demeanor,</i>

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:59.000
<i>I caught a glimpse
of the boy's long fight against illness.</i>

00:16:00.710 --> 00:16:02.830
<i>Shogi is honest.</i>

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:05.710
<i>The only way to get good at it is by studying.</i>

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:11.680
<i>That's right. What I had in my hand
were the game records</i>

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:18.060
<i>of someone who threw
a happy childhood to the winds.</i>

00:16:19.810 --> 00:16:21.600
<i>No, that's not right.</i>

00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:29.860
<i>He never even had the kind of childhood
that could be flung away.</i>

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:42.170
It's huge.

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:48.130
<i>There is No Correct Answer
for Shogi...</i>

00:16:54.430 --> 00:16:56.470
Sh-Shimada 6th-Dan!

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:59.600
That's okay. Lie down.

00:17:00.060 --> 00:17:02.560
I've come in our mentor's place for today.

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:05.060
He's got nerve pain right now,
so he can't move.

00:17:05.810 --> 00:17:07.070
Excited to see an actual professional shogi player

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:09.570
Here, these are from him.

00:17:10.490 --> 00:17:12.400
He said they're old, but hope that's okay.

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:15.820
Treasure Island

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:15.820
20,000 Leagues
Under the Sea

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:15.820
They're illustrated first editions!

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:21.200
<i>When I asked him if he wanted to play...</i>

00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:23.830
Really?!

00:17:24.620 --> 00:17:27.130
<i>...some color came to his pasty face.</i>

00:17:35.470 --> 00:17:39.350
<i>And so I would play him from time to time.</i>

00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:48.980
<i>He would always give it everything he had</i>

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:53.990
<i>and beating him always required much effort.</i>

00:18:00.450 --> 00:18:04.370
<i>But one day, I hurt him.</i>

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.460
<i>His health had taken a turn for the worse</i>

00:18:07.460 --> 00:18:12.300
<i>and he'd been on a losing streak,
so the idea was to encourage him.</i>

00:18:13.050 --> 00:18:16.220
Please don't hold back like that!

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:17.140
Kiddo.

00:18:17.430 --> 00:18:21.350
If I'm treated as a "weakling"
even when I play shogi,

00:18:21.890 --> 00:18:25.730
where am I supposed to live?!

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:37.200
<i>His disease is incurable,
so it would be with him for the rest of his life.</i>

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:40.410
Kiddo, I'm sorry.

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:44.160
I'll never do it again, I promise.

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:50.170
<i>He had strict dietary restrictions.</i>

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:55.420
<i>His days went by enduring, holding his breath,
and hoping his condition wouldn't deteriorate.</i>

00:18:56.680 --> 00:19:01.930
<i>He could hardly do anything. Fighting, sports,
playing with friends were all out of the question.</i>

00:19:03.220 --> 00:19:06.690
<i>The only place
where he could run about as a hero</i>

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:12.570
<i>were on the 81 squares of this game board.</i>

00:19:18.240 --> 00:19:22.700
Kiriyama. These are the game records
of today's semi-finals.

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:36.460
HARUNOBU NIKAIDOU

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:42.470
Brother, please don't tell Kiriyama
about my disease.

00:19:43.720 --> 00:19:47.730
To get stronger, a rival is essential.

00:19:48.180 --> 00:19:52.650
He doesn't realize it himself,
but he's a kind person.

00:19:53.690 --> 00:19:55.570
And he's unstable.

00:19:57.110 --> 00:20:00.320
If he knew about this, he'd lose his touch.

00:20:01.570 --> 00:20:04.830
Then I wouldn't be able...

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:08.460
...to get any better.

00:20:10.120 --> 00:20:11.880
<i>The game record was two pages.</i>

00:20:12.630 --> 00:20:15.380
<i>The first match,
where he used all the time available.</i>

00:20:19.800 --> 00:20:22.720
<i>He was in the inferior position,
but he stuck it out,</i>

00:20:22.970 --> 00:20:24.890
<i>and right as he turned it around
with an upper hand,</i>

00:20:26.390 --> 00:20:28.390
<i>his opponent had a threefold repetition.</i>

00:20:29.890 --> 00:20:32.020
<i>Near the end of the ensuing rematches...</i>

00:20:33.480 --> 00:20:39.490
<i>After 138 moves that wrung out his soul,
with only one minute allowed per move...</i>

00:21:05.140 --> 00:21:11.140
Kiriyama. Even so,
can you be merciless to Nikaidou?

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:29.990
I'm going to the finals.

00:21:33.500 --> 00:21:34.420
All right.

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:39.420
<i>The Newcomer Tournament finals
were held a week later</i>

00:21:39.710 --> 00:21:41.720
<i>at the Kansai Shogi Hall.</i>

00:21:52.270 --> 00:21:54.480
Crap. It's really coming down.

00:21:55.150 --> 00:21:57.560
Well, we're near the train station.

00:21:57.900 --> 00:21:59.110
Make a run for it?

00:21:59.110 --> 00:22:00.070
Okay.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:07.780
<i>As we were running in the rain
that looked like thin, silver threads,</i>

00:22:08.030 --> 00:22:13.290
<i>I thought back on Nikaidou's game records.</i>

00:22:17.000 --> 00:22:21.050
<i>Though he was hesitant
and faltered and flinched,</i>

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:28.010
<i>he had faith in himself,</i>

00:22:31.390 --> 00:22:33.520
<i>so he aimed for the "promised land"</i>

00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:37.270
<i>and raced ahead like a fireball.</i>

00:22:48.160 --> 00:22:49.740
<i>Those two pages...</i>

00:22:52.200 --> 00:22:54.450
<i>...read like an adventure novel.</i>

00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:00.040
Adventurers

00:24:30.010 --> 00:24:32.010
Next Episode Preview

00:24:32.010 --> 00:24:37.810
Episode 31

00:24:32.430 --> 00:24:34.890
Nikaidou kept playing
until he collapsed.

00:24:35.140 --> 00:24:37.810
And the girl in front of me...

00:24:38.060 --> 00:24:40.770
I have a feeling I have to go.

00:24:40.980 --> 00:24:44.060
I swear I'll win
before coming back home.

00:24:44.360 --> 00:24:47.030
Thank you, Kiriyama.

00:24:47.610 --> 00:24:50.030
Huh? Where am I?

00:24:50.030 --> 00:24:58.750
ILLUSTRATION:
HAJIME UEDA

00:24:51.910 --> 00:24:57.540
Kiriyama, next time let's have dinner
together with Kiddo.
